mothershipOS: the external camera HAL drives a mothershipOS host camera's focus and light through the device's standard
V4L2 controls (FOCUS_AUTO, FOCUS_ABSOLUTE, AUTO_FOCUS_START/STATUS, FLASH_LED_MODE; mship.camera): AF modes off
(manual focus distance), auto (triggered) and continuous with the host's real AF state, flash for captures,
torch (setTorchMode). A device without these controls keeps the stock fixed-focus, no-flash behaviour.

